<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Urumqi</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Dihua</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Urumqi is the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xinjiang">Xinjiang</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uyghurs">Uyghur</a> Autonomous Region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, lying in an oasis on the northern side of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tian-shan">Tian Shan</a>. A small settlement in earlier centuries, it grew after the Qing conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dzungaria">Dzungaria</a> in the 1750s as a garrison town called Dihua, and became the provincial capital in 1884. It is now the largest city of Xinjiang.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/urumqi.jpg" alt="Urumqi" width="320" height="181" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Albertaont · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Urumqi_Skyline_July_2019.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
